WEBVTT

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.950
From the Secretary of Defense to the people of the United States,

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.620
this is the annual report of our armed forces.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.750
Your narrator, Peter Hackes, Pentagon reporter,

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.180
with the ABCs of a year of crisis in Asia, in Berlin, in Cuba,

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.510
and how our armed forces have met and are meeting these challenges to freedom.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.940
In their drive for world domination, the communists have identified different levels of possible conflict to exploit.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.600
Khrushchev speaks of war and peace in the light of what he calls the new means of mass destruction.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.660
What Mr. Khrushchev calls local wars, he also rejects.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.640
Because, as he puts it, they may grow into a thermonuclear war.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:16.200
Khrushchev recognizes another category, which he calls wars of liberation and popular revolt,

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:20.190
but which we prefer to call subversion and covert aggression.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.220
It is these wars which Khrushchev says are not only admissible, but inevitable.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.720
Free World's Answer.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:40.990
tested during a year in vietnam is counterinsurgency at the request of the south vietnamese government

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:48.630
we are helping peace-loving people learn how to defend themselves here in a remote setting

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:53.720
there is new emphasis on the importance of the individual fighting man as a teacher

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:54.920
as well as a leader.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:59.960
Our troops are here to...

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:05.630
advise and train the South Vietnamese, but fight only to defend themselves on assignments

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.910
which often take them into the midst of a bitter and dangerous struggle.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.460
In this conflict, it is harder to find the enemy than to fight him.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:28.130
Reaction time to guerrilla attack has been cut from hours to minutes with faster air

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.830
transport and improved communication.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.100
South Vietnamese troops round up an enemy who strikes quickly and brutally,

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:42.490
who already has assassinated countless civilian leaders, teachers, and other villagers who refuse to join them.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.820
The plan to protect those who dwell in thousands of rural villages and towns

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:53.920
resulted in the fortifying of approximately 5,000 communities in the first year.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.490
During an intensive visit to Southeast Asia,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.720
Secretary of Defense Robert S. McNamara sees how the fortified Hamlet program is working out.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:13.880
The Home Guard, like the Volunteer Fire Department, is constantly on the alert against brush fire surprise attacks,

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.420
which flare up whenever Viet Cong raiders are in the vicinity.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.560
Bamboo spiked parapets may seem a primitive barrier, but are effective against night raiders.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:47.740
Sure, our Navy has trained South Vietnamese Navy junk patrols, which guard internal waterways too.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.020
These patrols halt suspicious vessels for search and interrogation.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:05.820
Distinguishing between friend and communist foe is one of the most difficult problems of guerrilla war.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:20.020
Overhead, the U.S. Air Force trains South Vietnamese pilots to supply isolated outposts in a land where roads are all too few.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:29.970
In tactical operations, the experience and support of our Air Force...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.420
force-trained South Vietnamese pilots give confidence and wings to government

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:47.850
troops. Air commandos, like their counterparts in the Army and Navy, are

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.170
trained for special missions. They also act as instructors and advisors.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.320
and on-the-spot training call for dedication from the man in the field to the top commander,

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.220
General Paul D. Harkins.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:13.050
The U.S. effort to our Vietnamese allies is a vast and comprehensive one.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:18.290
It involves political, economic, psychological, and military measures.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.850
All of the armed forces of the U.S. play a part.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.970
On this side of the world, less than 90 miles from Florida,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.300
we faced another communist challenge, one that caused a world crisis.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.290
In the president's own words.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:41.090
This government, as promised, has maintained the closest surveillance

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:45.730
of the Soviet military buildup on the island of Cuba.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:51.320
Within the past week, unmistakable evidence has established the fact

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:58.730
that a series of offensive missile sites is now in preparation on that imprisoned island.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.110
The purpose of these bases can be none other than to provide a nuclear strike capability

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.100
against the Western Hemisphere.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:16.410
To halt this offensive buildup, a strict quarantine on all offensive military equipment

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.190
under shipment to Cuba is being initiated.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:26.380
All ships of any kind bound for Cuba from whatever nation or port where they're found

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.200
to contain cargoes of offensive weapons be turned back.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:35.520
Secretary of Defense McNamara announcing the quarantine order tells the press.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:40.570
Those are the instructions we've been given. Those are the instructions we will carry out.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:49.360
Soviet Chairman Khrushchev decided to dismantle the bases in Cuba and to remove the offensive weapons.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:59.980
Under Navy surveillance, the missiles that had threatened the U.S.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:09.620
went back where they came from. Later, the Soviet bombers, which the president listed as offensive

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:23.820
weapons, also were shipped home from Cuba. In Florida, the Commander-in-Chief sighted Air Force,

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:27.940
Navy, and Marine Corps units, which flew the surveillance missions that revealed the

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.240
communist missile buildup.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.140
Again, high- and low-level reconnaissance pilots emphasized individual skill and achievement

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.990
as they flew these important historic missions.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:48.370
The President also inspected the ground forces massed in Florida, ready for any action required.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:59.980
Guantanamo Naval Base, the U.S. Marines reinforced the...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:10.040
local garrison. Again, the individual fighting man became a symbol to the world of America's

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:22.110
determination to deter all communist aggression. Earlier in Asia, because communist attacks in

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:27.780
Laos threatened the border of Thailand, the U.S. responded quickly when Thailand called for help.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:39.030
Our 7th fleet landed combat-ready marines in Bangkok, in our biggest military move in the Far East since the Korean War.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:52.140
Army combat units were flown in by the Air Force to reinforce army troops already in Thailand on maneuvers.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:57.380
The soldiers moved in along the Thai frontier facing communist-infiltrated Laos.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.980
The presence of our military forces at...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.910
critical moment was sufficient to deter and open communist aggression against peaceful Thailand.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:17.740
Again, in India, when communist Chinese attacked in aggression reminiscent of Korea,

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:28.800
U.S. help was prompt. Here, the Air Force flew in urgently needed arms at the request of India's

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:29.100
government.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:52.080
In Asia, ability to deter aggression has been improving steadily through increased cooperation with our allies of CETO, the Southeast Asia Treaty Organization.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.980
In the South China Sea, Exercise Sea Devil brought together...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.500
other Navy units from Australia, New Zealand, Pakistan, Thailand, the United Kingdom, and our

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:23.920
own Seventh Fleet. And the sailors of Six Nations stress teamwork as well as individual skill. From

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:28.060
the Bamboo Curtain to the Berlin Wall, we are maintaining our commitments.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:35.440
standing firmly with our allies against communist designs for world conquest.

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:46.550
This wall has become a clear-cut symbol of tyranny in modern times.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:58.000
Our forces hold constant alerts to maintain this frontier of freedom,

00:10:58.660 --> 00:10:59.960
and each soldier realizes...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.960
the importance of his own role.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:29.820
Despite periodic delays, our forces maintain their right to travel

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:32.890
through communist East Germany to reach West Berlin.

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:36.490
The red flag, a constant reminder of the danger

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:38.130
that threatens every free man.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:43.610
Directing the men on our global frontiers

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:44.610
are the men at the Pentagon.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:48.320
Our $50 billion defense program is explained

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:50.600
by Secretary of Defense McNamara.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.230
The past year, we've doubled the rate

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.490
of building Polaris submarines.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.800
We've doubled capacity to produce Minutemen.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:07.020
missiles. We've increased airlift and tactical fighter procurement by 100%. We've tripled the

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:11.220
Army's special forces, and we've increased the number of Army's combat-ready divisions by nearly

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:18.820
50%, streamlined the military chain of command for faster action, and we've made the vital job

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:23.480
of recruiting, training, instructing, and equipping our fighting men the primary function of the

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:29.140
individual service secretaries. In concluding, I'd like to repeat General Marshall's words,

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:29.960
for I believe that

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.840
today they apply to every serviceman. General Marshall said, the soldier's

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:41.280
heart, the soldier's spirit, the soldier's soul are everything. Unless the soldier's

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:46.520
soul sustains him, he cannot be relied on. He'll fail himself, his commander, and his

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:52.580
country in the end. It's morale that wins the victory. It's staying power. The

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:59.100
spirit which endures to the end. The will to win. The Deputy Secretary of

00:12:59.100 --> 00:12:59.980
Defense is second.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.290
in command at the Pentagon. He shares the responsibility for shaping our overall military

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:11.830
power with Secretary McNamara on the top civilian management team, which includes the three service

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:18.600
secretaries. When Secretary McNamara is away from the Pentagon, the deputy is in charge. The

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:23.580
Secretary of the Army heads the department that provides the soldiers we need, whether it be for

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:28.480
counterinsurgency, civic action, conventional war, or tactical nuclear response.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:35.860
The Secretary of the Navy has the mission of ensuring that our Navy and Marine Corps

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:41.420
are capable of dealing with everything from the Cuban crisis and counterinsurgency to nuclear war.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:48.240
The Secretary of the Air Force, shown here welcoming home reservists, stresses their individual contributions.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:55.160
His job is to keep our Air Force ready for missions from aerial jungle warfare to deterring nuclear conflict.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.980
The top military team consists of the Joint Chiefs of the Army.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.240
Chiefs of Staff who direct our overall strategy and operations.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.660
General Wheeler represents the Army.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.290
Admiral Anderson is the Navy member.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.600
General LeMay heads the Air Force.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:20.210
And General Shoup is Commandant of the Marine Corps.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:24.030
The new Chairman is General Maxwell D. Taylor,

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.960
who assumed office October 1st, 1962.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:33.630
I'm looking forward with real anticipation to my new assignment in the Pentagon

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:36.340
and as service as chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:40.630
I find in this building, the old Pentagon, a new atmosphere

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:44.760
and a new approach to the problems of defense, which to me are most heartless.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:49.910
I refer to such things as the rediscovery of the need for conventional forces,

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:55.890
the recognition of subversive insurgency as an important form of modern conflict,

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:59.880
and the willingness to make hard decisions in the controversial areas.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:11.850
In recent years, the Secretary of Defense, through the Joint Chiefs of Staff, has directed the far-flung military operations of the unified commands composed of all services.

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:18.980
Also, there are specified commands, which means single-service commands, such as the Strategic Air Command.

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:27.240
There are nine in all. Depending on the military crisis of the moment, the Joint Chiefs can designate the appropriate command for action.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:36.270
The Atlantic Command, with headquarters at Norfolk, Virginia, handled the Cuban crisis with Admiral Dennison at the helm.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:47.160
The Pacific Command, with headquarters in Honolulu, handled Southeast Asia and the Far East with Admiral Felt in overall charge.

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:54.790
The European Command, with headquarters in Paris, is closely associated with the Supreme Command of NATO.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:57.110
Both are led by General Lemnitzer.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:05.440
Strike Command, located at Tampa, Florida, the newest unified command, is under General Adams.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:11.580
Combat elements of the Army and Air Force are prepared to strike hard and fast anywhere in the world.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:22.020
SAC, Strategic Air Command, is a nuclear deterrent to war with its tremendous second strike or counterpunch capability.

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:29.580
Bombers at the Strategic Air Command are constantly alert.

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:38.700
ready to respond to presidential command protection for civilians on the home front

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:44.600
is the responsibility of civil defense the national survey marking and stocking program

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:50.460
has located potential shelter spaces for more than 100 million americans by 1968

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:55.680
the program is expected to provide shelter spaces for Americans at home or at work.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:07.100
The Women's Army Corps and Sister Services, the WAVES, WAFs, and Women Marines,

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:11.560
continue their fine work as an integral part of our defense forces.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:19.820
And a century after Clara Barton of the American Red Cross helped the wounded in this Civil War setting,

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:24.870
the traditional role of nurses in war and peace has expanded around the world.

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:29.970
During the past year, Army nurses...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.300
went to earthquake-shattered Iran, where U.S. field hospitals ministered to the victims.

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:43.650
Air Force planes flew in vitally needed shelter and other supplies,

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:48.700
as they have done for a dozen countries stricken by earthquakes, famine, or flood.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.420
On other missions of health, as part of our assistance program,

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:07.500
The defense has flown supplies via the Air Force and distributed by the Army to strengthen the economy and security of new nations in Africa.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:13.780
Such supplies to interior African republics help new governments to prevent subversion by communism.

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:29.000
Since the Berlin crisis of 1961, the nation relies more than ever upon its citizen soldiers, sailors and airmen.

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:41.680
The first reservists, returning in 1962 after a year of active duty, were greeted informally by the commander-in-chief.

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:46.860
148,000 reservists and National Guardsmen responded to this call.

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:52.790
Each realized he was an important individual whose skill answered his nation's need.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:05.900
the National Guard and Reserves, announced in December 1962, will provide more combat-ready

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:14.270
units, streamlined to meet Cold War requirements of the future. Physical fitness as well as mental

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:24.220
alertness is still basic for all who serve in our armed forces. The Air Force includes missile men

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:29.960
as well as flyers. Here at Malmstrom Air Force Base, a strategic missile wing controls the most

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:37.100
modern Minuteman in its underground silo. The Air Force specialists on this job, by continuous

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:46.370
readiness to launch their bird, help prevent rather than start a nuclear war. In addition to missiles,

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:52.360
manned flying is still of primary importance in a balanced Air Force. Now and in the foreseeable

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:57.600
future, the Air Force is calling for pilots who must have the split-second precision and skill

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:59.300
of its famed Thunderbirds.

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:09.320
already on the drawing board for the future is tfx tactical fighter experimental to be delivered

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:15.780
within two and a half years the f-111a designed for air force and navy use will be a tactical

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:21.860
fighter capable of supersonic speed the decision to develop one fighter for both services is

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:28.160
expected to save approximately one billion dollars meanwhile the services are purchasing

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.810
the phantom jet the nation

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:37.260
finest tactical plane already in operation. The Navy and Marine Corps call this the F-4B and the

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:44.120
Air Force calls its version the F-4C. The Navy, like the Air Force, calls for scientists as well

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:49.540
as flyers and sailors, but insists on individual fitness to meet the requirements of a modern

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:57.960
Navy. In the past year, two nuclear submarines surfaced at the North Pole after traveling under

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.920
the polar ice pack to the top of the

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:08.230
world. The skippers of the Skate and Sea Dragon exchange greetings on the ice in another achievement

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:15.840
demonstrating the far-ranging mobility of the nuclear submarine fleet. We are increasing the

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:29.440
number of Polaris submarines. By late 1964 or early 1965, we'll have 29 in commission. Two crews,

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.120
The blue and the gold alternate on these subs, going out on undersea patrol for 60 days at a time.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:48.540
This year, more fleet ballistic missile submarines increase our nuclear deterrent powers on the seven seas.

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:53.960
On station, each is ready to fire Polaris missiles from hidden launching platforms.

00:21:58.270 --> 00:21:59.970
Today's surface Navy in

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.000
It includes nuclear-powered ships like the aircraft carrier Enterprise, now in full operation,

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:11.880
cruiser Long Beach, and the guided-missile frigate Bainbridge.

00:22:15.010 --> 00:22:23.250
The USS Albany firing three missiles simultaneously represents a sizable force of cruisers armed with one or more types of missiles.

00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:34.560
The Navy, too, is training small units for lonely and dangerous missions.

00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:39.400
Men who must perform a variety of skills, often in more than one environment.

00:22:46.740 --> 00:22:50.620
Like the guerrilla soldier, the frogman on an underwater demolition team

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:55.940
must prove his ability and courage during a long, extensive, and difficult period of training.

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:07.710
Great emphasis in 1962 was given to the Army's Special Forces, a select group of individual fighting men.

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:15.360
These U.S. guerrilla fighters are twice volunteers, first as paratroopers, then for hazardous duty with Special Forces.

00:23:18.100 --> 00:23:20.820
They have been trained, retrained, and cross-trained.

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:27.430
They can do everything from parachuting behind enemy lines to teaching school to killing sentries with the heel of their hand.

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:36.940
Knowledge and techniques in guerrilla warfare are being shared constantly with our partners

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:42.180
in this hemisphere. In the Canal Zone, the Caribbean Command holds a conference of American

00:23:42.180 --> 00:23:54.590
armies attended by officers from various Latin American countries. Back at the Inter-American

00:23:54.590 --> 00:23:59.870
Defense College in Washington, our friends from south of the border take high-level staff courses.

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:05.460
which range from conventional war to meeting the guerrilla challenges of Castro-type communists.

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:15.350
In Asia, in South Vietnam, we are learning as well as teaching.

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:23.420
Here, communist infiltration and subversion still are seeking to destroy South Vietnam with guerrilla hit-and-run warfare.

00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:35.620
as the free vietnamese fortify their villages against the attacks of gorillas this warfare

00:24:35.620 --> 00:24:42.340
becomes strongly reminiscent of the american past then as now isolated communities in danger

00:24:42.340 --> 00:24:48.790
of sudden attack were forced to protect themselves once more fighting is on a primitive level the

00:24:49.010 --> 00:24:55.230
techniques are those of the indian fighter the scout move silently use the concealment of woods

00:24:55.350 --> 00:24:58.840
Swamp or jungle, strike fast and hard.

00:25:01.340 --> 00:25:08.110
Francis Marion, the Swamp Fox, and before him, Rogers Rangers.

00:25:08.710 --> 00:25:13.450
There have been many precedents in our history for some of the fighting methods demanded today.

00:25:15.350 --> 00:25:19.030
Guerrilla warfare is a new challenge, but an age-old technique.

00:25:20.540 --> 00:25:26.940
Like the warrior of yesterday, the individual fighting man of today must be ready for anything at any time.

00:25:31.820 --> 00:25:36.530
We cannot forget that behind all of our defense effort is the individual man.

00:25:37.060 --> 00:25:43.100
In guerrilla warfare, no machine can replace his judgment, his courage, or his will to win.

00:25:45.630 --> 00:25:50.750
In the peaceful exploration of space directed by NASA, the National Aeronautics and Space

00:25:50.750 --> 00:25:56.260
Administration, the Army, Navy, Air Force, and Marine Corps provide support with equipment,

00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:58.280
missile boosters, and manpower.

00:25:58.280 --> 00:25:59.980
Here is Lieutenant Colonel...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.740
John H. Glenn Jr. of the Marine Corps, the first American to orbit the Earth, an outstanding space

00:26:05.740 --> 00:26:11.830
achievement in 1962. All astronauts to date are from the Navy, Air Force, and Marine Corps.

00:26:14.010 --> 00:26:19.220
While supporting peaceful missions in space, we cannot neglect our military missiles and

00:26:19.220 --> 00:26:26.010
defense technology on Earth. The Minuteman, which became operational in 1962, has a range of more

00:26:26.010 --> 00:26:29.960
than 6,000 miles. The latest Army missile for troops...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:36.110
use is the Pershing, a shoot and scoot missile with a 300-mile range. For every level of conflict,

00:26:36.230 --> 00:26:47.780
we are maintaining a balanced defense. The Air Force Atlas, one of SAC's operational missiles,

00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:53.540
is also very much on the job. It doesn't look real, but this is the actual film of

00:26:53.540 --> 00:26:59.460
an Atlas separating from its booster in space, literally out of this world. It was taken by a

00:26:59.460 --> 00:26:59.860
special

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:11.110
high-speed camera inside the atlas itself. The commander-in-chief in his 1963 message on the

00:27:11.110 --> 00:27:18.450
State of the Union sums up our military position. This country, therefore, continues to require

00:27:18.450 --> 00:27:25.350
the best defense in the world, a defense which is suited to the 60s. This means, unfortunately,

00:27:25.710 --> 00:27:29.540
a rising defense budget, for there is no substitute for

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:37.810
adequate defense and no bargain basement way of achieving it. It means the expenditure of more

00:27:37.810 --> 00:27:45.270
than 15 billion dollars this year on nuclear weapons systems alone, a sum which is about equal

00:27:45.270 --> 00:27:52.720
to the combined defense budgets of our European allies, but it also means improved air and

00:27:52.720 --> 00:27:59.920
missile defenses, improved civil defense, a strengthened anti-guerrilla capacity, and of

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:06.980
prime importance more powerful and flexible non-nuclear forces. For threats of massive

00:28:06.980 --> 00:28:15.100
retaliation may not deter piecemeal aggression and a line of destroyers in a quarantine or a

00:28:15.100 --> 00:28:21.500
division of well-equipped men on a border may be more useful to our real security than the

00:28:21.500 --> 00:28:29.080
multiplication of awesome weapons beyond all rational need. It makes little sense for us to assail

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:37.800
speeches and resolutions the horrors of communism to spend fifty billion dollars a year to prevent

00:28:37.800 --> 00:28:45.940
its military advance and then to begrudge spending largely on american products less than one-tenth

00:28:45.940 --> 00:28:52.840
of that amount to help other nations strengthen their independence and cure the social chaos

00:28:52.840 --> 00:28:55.780
in which communism has always thrived.

00:28:57.370 --> 00:28:59.030
The Nassau Agreement recognizes

00:28:59.030 --> 00:28:59.510
that

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:04.140
the security of the West is indivisible, and so must be our defense.

00:29:05.160 --> 00:29:11.320
There are, in fact, nearly one million Americans serving their country and the cause of freedom

00:29:11.320 --> 00:29:15.960
in overseas posts, a record no other people can match.

00:29:16.580 --> 00:29:22.240
I think these are proud and memorable days in the cause of peace and freedom.

00:29:23.240 --> 00:29:29.280
We are proud, for example, of Major Rudolph Anderson, who gave his life over the island

00:29:29.280 --> 00:29:29.760
of Cuba.

00:29:36.940 --> 00:29:42.590
We salute specialist James Allen Johnson, who died on the border of South Korea.

00:29:47.630 --> 00:29:51.400
Pay honor to the Sergeant Gerald Pendle, who was killed in Vietnam.

00:29:56.280 --> 00:29:59.100
They are among the many who in this century...

00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:02.870
far from home, have died for our country.

00:30:04.090 --> 00:30:06.810
Our task now, and the task of all Americans,

00:30:07.580 --> 00:30:08.980
is to live up to their commitment.

00:30:10.580 --> 00:30:15.010
With thanks to Almighty God for seeing us through a perilous passage,

00:30:16.130 --> 00:30:19.900
we ask his help anew in guiding the good ship union.

00:30:22.100 --> 00:30:25.400
The United States can be proud of our armed forces,

00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:27.820
alert to meet every challenge,

00:30:28.540 --> 00:30:29.980
the spirit that safeguards...

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:40.780
our country is the will to serve and the will to win of everyone in uniform. Each knows the

00:30:40.780 --> 00:30:47.220
mission, defense of freedom everywhere, which means defense of our own America.
